        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq2">
            How do I prepare for a CER audit?
            <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq2">You need complete installation records for every solar job: signed customer consent, compliant wiring diagrams, correct STC assignment forms, and evidence of AS/NZS 5033 compliance. Ask Tradie Brain AI for a pre-audit checklist specific to your business setup and it will walk you through it step by step.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq3">
            What is the CCEW 7-day rule in NSW?
            <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq3">NSW electricians must lodge a Certificate of Compliance Electrical Work (CCEW) within 7 days of completing any electrical installation. Failure to lodge is a breach under the Home Building Act 1989 and can attract fines. Tradie Brain AI can explain what triggers a CCEW, how to handle partial completions, and how to manage lodgement at scale.</div>
