              <div class="lib-qa-body" id="qa-5-2">
                <p>ServiceM8 has a native Xero integration:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Connect:</strong> ServiceM8 → Add-ons → Xero → Authorize. Both apps must be active with valid subscriptions.</li>
                  <li><strong>Account mapping:</strong> Map ServiceM8 labour and material line items to the correct Xero accounts and tax codes (typically 15% GST for standard solar installs)</li>
                  <li><strong>Invoice sync:</strong> Set whether invoices sync to Xero on creation, approval, or payment — most solar businesses use approval to allow for review</li>
                  <li><strong>Payments:</strong> Xero payments can sync back to ServiceM8 to mark jobs as paid — reduces double-handling</li>
                  <li><strong>Customer records:</strong> Customers created in ServiceM8 sync to Xero contacts automatically</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Common issue: GST codes mismatched. STC rebate values passed through to customers should be mapped to the correct account — ask your accountant how to treat STC assignment value in Xero before setting up the integration.</p>
                <button class="lib-ask-btn" data-prompt="How do I set up Xero integration in ServiceM8 for a solar installation business?">⚡ Ask about ServiceM8 Xero integration</button>
