            <div class="lib-qa">
              <button class="lib-qa-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="qa-5-5" data-prompt="How do I handle a negative Google review as a solar or electrical contractor in Australia?">
                How should I respond to a negative Google review?
                <svg class="lib-qa-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
              </button>
              <div class="lib-qa-body" id="qa-5-5">
                <p>A good response to a negative review is read by every future customer who sees it — it's marketing, not damage control:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Respond within 24–48 hours</strong> — shows you're attentive</li>
                  <li><strong>Acknowledge, don't argue</strong> — even if the review is unfair, publicly arguing looks worse than the review itself</li>
                  <li><strong>Template:</strong> "Hi [name], thanks for taking the time to leave feedback. We're sorry to hear you had this experience. We take [issue] seriously and would like to make it right — please contact us directly on [phone] so we can resolve this for you."</li>
                  <li><strong>Move it offline</strong> — never go back and forth in review replies; get it to a private channel</li>
                  <li><strong>Flag if fake:</strong> If you believe the review is from someone who was never a customer, flag it through Google Business Profile for removal</li>
                </ul>
                <p>The best protection against negative reviews is a high volume of positive ones. Set up your review automation (above) so every happy customer gets a prompt.</p>
                <button class="lib-ask-btn" data-prompt="How should I respond to a negative Google review as a solar or electrical contractor in Australia?">⚡ Ask about handling negative reviews</button>
